# KDP Blurb Writer

A local-first Python CLI that writes Kindle Direct Publishing (KDP) book blurbs from a short premise,
using a configurable OpenAI-compatible endpoint (default: Ollama running on localhost).

Built and maintained by **Asdale Dynamics, LLC** — beginner-friendly AI education, books, guides,
and practical tools. Learn more at dylanasdale.github.io.

## What it does

Feed it a one-sentence premise and it returns a finished KDP blurb: hook, conflict, stakes, and a
call to action, in the tone and length you choose. Print it to the terminal or export it straight to
Markdown.

No API keys required. No account needed. Everything runs against your own endpoint, so your book
ideas stay on your machine. If you just want to try it out, the built-in mock provider generates
realistic blurbs without calling any model at all.

## Install

```bash
git clone <this-repo>
cd kdp-blurb-writer-cli
pip install -e .
```

This installs the `kdp-blurb-writer` command. Python 3.9+ required. No external dependencies — only
the Python standard library.

## Usage

```bash
# Print a blurb to the terminal (uses the mock provider, no server needed)
kdp-blurb-writer "A registered nurse discovers a time-traveling stethoscope" --mock --tone warm --length medium

# Pick a tone and length
kdp-blurb-writer "AI agents that run your small business" --mock --tone professional --length long

# Export to Markdown
kdp-blurb-writer "A chess prodigy from nowhere" --mock --out blurb.md

# Point it at your own Ollama endpoint
kdp-blurb-writer "A gardener teaches robots to grow food" --endpoint http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions --model llama3.2
```

Options:

| Option | Default | Meaning |
|--------|---------|---------|
| `premise` | (required) | Your short book premise or idea |
| `--tone` | `warm` | `professional`, `warm`, `hype`, `mysterious`, `minimal`, `friendly` |
| `--length` | `medium` | `short`, `medium`, `long` |
| `--endpoint` | `http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions` | OpenAI-compatible chat completions URL |
| `--model` | (empty) | Model name; Ollama works without it |
| `--out` | — | Write the blurb to a Markdown file |
| `--mock` | off | Use the built-in deterministic mock provider |

## Example output

Premise: *A nurse discovers a time-traveling stethoscope*

> When a nurse discovers a time-traveling stethoscope, everything changes.
>
> Caught between impossible choices and stakes she never saw coming, the journey ahead
> demands courage, heart, and a willingness to risk it all.
>
> Discover a story that stays with you long after the final page.
>
> Scroll up and grab your copy today.

## Testing

```bash
pip install -e .
python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
```

Tests use the mock provider only — no network, no keys, no secrets.

## Values

- **Local-first**: your premises and blurbs never leave your machine unless you point the CLI at a remote endpoint yourself.
- **No secrets**: no API keys, no personal data, no telemetry.
- **Plain English**: built for beginners, written to be read like a friend explaining it.

